":"SVRPUB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nNorthwestern Baca County in southeastern Colorado...\nEast central Las Animas County in southeastern Colorado...\nSouthern Bent County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 530 PM MDT.\n\n* At 441 PM MDT, severe thunderstorms were located along a line\nextending from 23 miles south of Higbee to 11 miles east of Kim to\n19 miles northwest of Kenton, moving northeast at 35 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Golf ball size hail and 60 mph wind gusts.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...People and animals outdoors will be injured. Expect hail\ndamage to roofs, siding, windows, and vehicles. Expect\nwind damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nPritchett and Kim.","ends":"2026-08-15T17:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Baca, CO; Bent, CO; Las Animas, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.210edc1de551f2823fd34e54fb993c3059815bd4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.210edc1de551f2823fd34e54fb993c3059815bd4.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 15 at 2:05PM MDT until August 15 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n584 IN EFFECT UNTIL 9 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING AREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 9 COUNTIES\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nEL PASO\n\nIN SOUTHEAST COLORADO\n\nBACA                  BENT                  CROWLEY\nKIOWA                 LAS ANIMAS            OTERO\nPROWERS               PUEBLO\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF COLORADO SPRINGS, EADS, LA JUNTA,\nLAMAR, LAS ANIMAS, OLNEY SPRINGS, ORDWAY,\nPETERSON SPACE FORCE BASE, PUEBLO, ROCKY FORD, SPRINGFIELD,\nTRINIDAD, AND WALSH.","ends":"2026-08-15T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Baca, CO; Bent, CO; Crowley, CO; El Paso, CO; Kiowa, CO; Las Animas, CO; Otero, CO; Prowers, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ab34da50e8fd205d61f13d5bcbb1589d5f873cbb.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ab34da50e8fd205d61f13d5bcbb1589d5f873cbb.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 4:59PM MDT until August 15 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central, east central, and southeast Colorado,\nincluding the following areas, Teller, El Paso, Huerfano, Las\nAnimas, Crowley, Otero, Kiowa, Bent and Prowers Counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Abundant monsoon moisture will result in scattered to numerous\nthunderstorms this afternoon and evening which will be capable of\nproducing heavy rainfall and flash flooding, especially for urban\nareas or locations with already saturated soil conditions.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-15T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Teller County/Rampart Range above 7500fT/Pike's Peak Between 7500 And 11000 Ft; Pikes Peak above 11000 Ft; Northern El Paso County/Monument Ridge/Rampart Range Below 7500 Ft; Colorado Springs Vicinity/Southern El Paso County/Rampart Range Below 7400 Ft; Walsenburg Vicinity/Upper Huerfano River Basin Below 7500 Ft; Trinidad Vicinity/Western Las Animas County Below 7500 Ft; Crowley County; La Junta Vicinity/Otero County; Eastern Las Animas County; Western Kiowa County; Eastern Kiowa County; Las Animas Vicinity/Bent County; Lamar Vicinity/Prowers County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756c47587b9063b4ff8ae253c038ec09a9c93d18.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.756c47587b9063b4ff8ae253c038ec09a9c93d18.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-15T19:12:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB